"Let $\\mathcal{S}^{(d)}_n$ be the set of $n$-vertex triangulations of the $d$-sphere, let $M(\\mathcal{S}^{(d)}_n)$ denote their minimum volume, and let $\\mu^{(d)}_n$ be the median of this random variable. **Minimum-volume scaling conjecture.** For every $d\\geq 2$ there is a constant $c_d>0$ such that\n\n$$\n\\mu^{(d)}_n = c_d n^{1-1/d} + o(n^{1-1/d}).\n$$\n\nThe conjecture asserts that the upper bound proved in the paper gives the correct asymptotic order and leading constant form. It is open even for $d=2$; in that case the available bounds constrain $c_2$ to an explicit interval."